		<Id>9000</Id>
		<Name>Citrix Hypervisor - Pool and Storage Inventory (Community Add-on)</Name>
		<IsMockTemplate>false</IsMockTemplate>
		<Description>This template complements SolarWinds' own "Citrix Hypervisor" Content Exchange template (63 host- and VM-level performance counters) rather than duplicating it. It adds pool-wide inventory facts that template does not cover: VM power-state counts, default storage repository capacity, snapshot age and count, and orphaned virtual disk detection, plus a handful of single-value host metrics (CPU, memory, one named physical interface, uptime, enabled/live status) built the same way that template's own components are.

Structure follows the proven format: one metric per component, each script prints exactly one "Statistic.&lt;Name&gt; : &lt;value&gt;" line matching its component's single DynamicEvidenceColumnSchema entry, and every LinuxScript component carries the same AuthenticationType, Port, ScriptDirectory and StatusRollupType settings that template uses.

Credentials: SSH access to a Linux host in the pool (dom0), with permission to run xe. Components documented "Inputs: None" self-discover the pool they are SSH'd into and need no configuration at assignment time; components documented with named inputs prompt for those values (for example XenServerHostname, InterfaceName) when the component is added to a node, exactly as SolarWinds' own Citrix Hypervisor template's host- and VM-level components do.

See docs/modules/sam-citrix-hypervisor-template.md in the SolarWinds_OrionGuides repository for what in this template is verified against a real Citrix Hypervisor host and what is not.</Description>
